# This scenario asserts on the three zone.slab_* counters, which only exist
# when the probe has a zone to report: with no `test_ref_zone` the document
# renders "zone":{"present":false} and every slab path is ABSENT, not zero.
#
# That absence is not a silent pass -- `probe`/`delta` over a missing path
# fails with "not present in document" -- but it fails for the wrong reason,
# reporting a harness misconfiguration in the language of a module defect. The
# zone is declared here so the counters are present and the assertions measure
# what they claim to.
#
# WHY THIS FILE DID NOT EXIST BEFORE. Every other assertion in this scenario
# watches the CYCLE POOL, which needs no zone, so the scenario ran zoneless
# from its creation until the slab counters were added. CI supplies
# PROBER_MODULE/DIRECTIVE/PROBE but never PROBER_PROBE_ZONE (it is per-scenario
# by design -- the reference module takes no zone by default, see
# t/module/ngx_http_test_ref_module.c's file header), so without this file the
# slab assertions would red on every remote leg while passing locally for
# anyone who happened to export the variable by hand.
#
# PROBER_PROBE is restated because mutate-suite-lib.sh defaults it and a
# scenario that overrides PROBER_PROBE_ZONE alone would lose the pairing --
# same reasoning as scenarios/zone-name-escaping/env, which is the other
# zone-carrying scenario and the model for this file.
#
# A plain name and a 1m size: this scenario tests allocation ACCOUNTING, not
# name escaping (that is zone-name-escaping's job) and not exhaustion (the
# fault_slab= knob's). 1m is far larger than the zero-allocation reference
# module will ever use, so slab_pages_free stays flat and a page-level change
# would be a real signal rather than sizing noise.
PROBER_PROBE="test_ref_probe;"
PROBER_PROBE_ZONE="test_ref_zone alloc_per_request 1m;"
